/*
:name: aeg_div_rem
:set: compile.cprop.engine=classic
:type: lec
*/
// PYROPE-vs-PYROPE group, the fixture of the aegraph Div/Rem rules (pass/aegraph/rules/div.rules, Q2).
// Dlop truncates toward zero and the remainder follows the DIVIDEND, so a power-of-two divisor is a shift /
// mask only for a non-negative dividend; `sq` / `sr` carry a NEGATIVE dividend and must keep the truncation.
// `qb` / `rb` / `qz` / `rz` are runtime divisors that can be ZERO (x / 0 and x % 0 are the all-unknown
// value, which the engine must not turn into a fixed result differently from classic). `qq` / `rr` are
// b / b and b % b. This is the REFERENCE, compiled by the classic engine; `aeg_div_rem_1.prp` is the
// same source compiled by the e-graph engine.
pub comb top(a:U8, s:S8, b:U8, z:U8) -> (q1:U8, q4:U6, r4:U2, q10:U5, r10:U4, sq:S8, sr:S8, qb:U8, rb:U8, qq:U8, rr:U8, qz:U8, rz:U8) {
  q1  = a / 1
  q4  = a / 4
  r4  = a % 4
  q10 = a / 10
  r10 = a % 10
  sq  = s / 4
  sr  = s % 4
  qb  = a / b
  rb  = a % b
  qq  = b / b
  rr  = b % b
  qz  = a / z
  rz  = a % z
}
